  "body": "Follow-up from #495 / PR #501. `assets/posts/sinumerik.cps` retracts with `G0 G53 Z0` before a tool change and `G53 Z0` at the end of the program. That assumes machine Z0 is the top of Z travel, which is usual on Siemens VMCs but still an assumption. On a machine homed elsewhere, the retract drives into the part, the same hazard as #495.\n\nPR #501 adds an optional machine-file key, `safe_retract` (the safe Z in machine coordinates), passed to post scripts as `machine.safeRetractZ`.\n\nDone means: `sinumerik.cps` reads `machine.safeRetractZ`. A stated value posts `G53 Z<v>`; with no machine or a stated 0, output is byte-identical to today. A machine that states a different home convention without a safe Z is refused by name, following the rule #501 settles for Tormach. Pinned by tests, with no Sinumerik golden changed.\n\nFanuc, Haas and Mazak use `G91 G28 Z0`, a return to the reference point, and are not affected.\n",
